# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository, whatever the working
# platform. Development happens on Windows and deployment is Linux (Railway);
# without this, files land in the index with mixed endings and every Prettier
# run produces a diff nobody asked for. Before this file existed the repo
# carried 217 CRLF-related lint errors.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git decide what is text; `eol=lf` fixes what it writes.
# Working copies are unaffected on Windows for editors that handle LF, which
# every editor in use here does.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binary. Never diffed, never normalised — a CRLF conversion inside any of
# these corrupts the file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.avif  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary

*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.eot   binary

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Text, but generated. Normalised like any other text file so they cannot
# reintroduce CRLF, and marked so they do not drown a review.
#
# NOT `binary` — that would stop normalisation, which is the opposite of what
# is wanted. `-diff` only suppresses the patch body; the file is still tracked,
# still merged, and still diffable with --text when someone actually needs it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
package-lock.json  -diff linguist-generated=true

# The Prisma client is generated into the repo (schema.prisma output setting)
# and is tracked. Its diffs are large, mechanical, and never reviewed.
backend/src/generated/**  -diff linguist-generated=true

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shell scripts must stay LF even on Windows checkouts — CRLF in a shebang
# script fails on Linux with the famously unhelpful "bad interpreter: no such
# file or directory".
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.sh  text eol=lf
